<title>MEXICO: Visa denies AMEX anti-competitive claims.</title>
<headline>Visa denies AMEX anti-competitive claims.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-09-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Credit card issuer Visa on Tuesday denied allegations by rival American Express that it is engaging in anti-competitive activities in five Latin American and Caribbean countries.</p>
<p>On Tuesday, American Express said it was filing legal complaints against Visa in Mexico, Argentina, Brazil and Colombia and had also sought an investigation of the firm in Puerto Rico.</p>
<p>It asserted that Visa has imposed a rule limiting competition between American Express and other card systems by restricting the products its members can offer customers. It said the Latin American board of Visa would adopt the bylaw next month.</p>
<p>In a statement issued in Mexico City, Visa said the claim was &quot;totally false&quot;. The company &quot;has not introduced any statute that prohibits members of Visa from emiting (credit) cards of the competition&quot;.</p>
<p>-- Henry Tricks, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9560</p>
